    {
      "number": 7,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 7,
      "stem": "A fixed segment $AB$ is 20 cm long. The point $X$ lies strictly to the right of $B$ on a horizontal ray. The angle $ABX$ is $45^\\circ$. The diagram is schematic.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find $BX$ when $AX$ is perpendicular to the ray.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find $BX$ when $AX=20$cm.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Find the two possible values of $BX$ when $AX=17$cm.",
          "marks": 4
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$10\\sqrt2$, $20\\sqrt2$; then $10\\sqrt2\\pm\\sqrt{89}$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use $\\cos45^\\circ=BX/20$ in the right triangle."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$BX=10\\sqrt2$cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$BX=20\\sqrt2$cm; the root $BX=0$ is excluded because $X\\ne B$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Apply the cosine rule to triangle $ABX$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$17^2=BX^2+20^2-40BX\\cos45^\\circ$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$BX=10\\sqrt2+\\sqrt{89}\\approx23.6$cm."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$BX=10\\sqrt2-\\sqrt{89}\\approx4.71$cm."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
        8
      ],
      "diagramSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 820 480\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A fixed segment and a point moving along a ray\"><rect width=\"820\" height=\"480\" fill=\"white\"/><text x=\"410\" y=\"27\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#111\">A fixed segment and a point moving along a ray</text><path d=\"M95 370L740 370\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M95 370L395 70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M395 70L620 370\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/><text x=\"95\" y=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#111\">B</text><text x=\"395\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#111\">A</text><text x=\"620\" y=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#111\">X</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#111\">20 cm</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#111\">45°</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#111\">X varies along the ray to the right of B; not to scale.</text></svg>"
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "section": "B",
      "marks": 12,
      "stem": "Points $B,A,Q$ lie in that order on a horizontal line, with $BA=1$ and $AQ=2$. Point $P$ is vertically above $Q$, with $PQ=x>0$. Let $\\alpha=\\angle PAQ$ and $\\beta=\\angle PBQ$. All angles are measured in degrees. Parts(a),(b),(c) describe separate positions of $P$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a(i)",
          "prompt": "Given $\\alpha=45^\\circ$, find $x$.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "a(ii)",
          "prompt": "For this position, find $\\beta$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Given $\\beta=40^\\circ$, find $\\alpha$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "c(i)",
          "prompt": "Now $\\angle APB=10^\\circ$. Show that $x=2\\tan\\alpha=3\\tan\\beta$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "c(ii)",
          "prompt": "Express $\\angle APB$ in terms of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "c(iii)",
          "prompt": "Find the two possible values of $x$.",
          "marks": 3
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$x=2$, $\\beta=33.7^\\circ$; $\\alpha=51.5^\\circ$; final $x=1.41$ or $4.26$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$x=2\\tan45^\\circ=2$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "a(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$\\tan\\beta=2/3$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\beta=33.690\\ldots^\\circ\\approx33.7^\\circ$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$x=3\\tan40^\\circ$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$x=2.517298\\ldots$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\alpha=\\tan^{-1}(x/2)=51.5327\\ldots^\\circ\\approx51.5^\\circ$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use right triangles $AQP$ and $BQP$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\tan\\alpha=x/2$ and $\\tan\\beta=x/3$, giving the result."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\angle APB=\\alpha-\\beta$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c(iii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Solve $2\\tan(10^\\circ+\\beta)=3\\tan\\beta$ for $0<\\beta<80^\\circ$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\beta=25.127\\ldots^\\circ$ or $54.872\\ldots^\\circ$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$x=3\\tan\\beta\\approx1.41$ or $4.26$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
